00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.409
Speaker 1: I want to revisit with you.

00:00:02.409 --> 00:00:03.939
Taxation is theft.

00:00:03.939 --> 00:00:09.840
It's the little brother to taxation is slavery
that we sometimes hear from Republicans and

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.430
right wingers.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:18.140
New congresswoman, a Republican, of course,
and Paulina Luna pulled out.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.849
Taxation is theft yesterday when being interviewed
on Fox Business by Neil CAVUTO.

00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:31.279
Let's listen and then discuss the endless
bottomless absurdity of this silly claim that

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:32.809
some Republicans like to make.

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:36.560
Speaker 2: I'm not going to say that I want
to cut defense spending, but I will say that

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.890
I think it's important that we are looking
to make sure that we are getting the best

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.789
deal, especially on some of the stuff that
we're spending money on.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:45.059
So I think that we need to have those discussions.

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:48.390
But more or less, what I've heard in some
of these negotiations is we're talking about

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:53.140
programs that aren't going to the necessities
that we, the American people, need, i.e.,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.140
protections.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:58.769
I'm talking about some of these woke ideology,
these funded programs, and for example, these

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:03.469
these salaries for these additional weaponized
87,000 IRS agents, which you saw, we tried

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:08.110
to pass yet the Senate and even the Biden
White House is pushing back on.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:13.060
Sir, I say taxation is theft and I don't want
any more IRS agents than you probably do.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:20.939
Speaker 1: So, wait, I'm going to restrict
this segment to taxation is theft because

00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:21.939
it's interesting.

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:22.939
Okay.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:27.780
So first of all, Anna, Paulina Luna salary
is paid by taxes.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:34.110
So if you really believe taxation is theft,
then you should be refusing your salary.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:40.329
You should reject such an ill gotten and stolen
salary if you actually believe that taxes

00:01:40.329 --> 00:01:45.040
are theft because you're being paid with stolen
money, sort of makes you an accessory to the

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.040
theft.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.040
That's number one.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.759
She's not rejecting her salary that I'm aware
of.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:52.790
But let's talk about taxation is theft.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:53.820
Taxation is theft.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.479
Every once in a while rears its ugly head,
usually among libertarian circles, but sometimes

00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:00.570
among reactionary MAGA as well.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.710
Taxation is not theft in a number of different
ways.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:13.160
First of all, nobody is forcing you to pay
taxes in the sense that you have the option

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.709
to work or not to work.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:17.620
Don't want to pay taxes, don't work.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.430
Oh, but then how would I fund my life?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.700
Well, you have a choice.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:27.770
Secondly, if you believe that the taxation
system in the United States is theft, you

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:32.320
can try to go to a different country that
might have a different system.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:38.069
What you might find is that the countries
in which you can get away with paying no taxes

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:40.170
aren't places you probably want to live.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:44.069
Now, you might say, Well, David, every every
country has taxes, so.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:48.610
Well, if your argument is the American government
is stealing through taxes, you're free to

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:52.310
try to go somewhere else if the immigration
law will allow you and if the tax law is more

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.630
favorable to you.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:03:01.510
Number three, you have decided to be here
in the sense that you either immigrated here

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:07.080
knowing that there are taxes in the United
States or your parents immigrated here and

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:13.630
then birthed you or your parents were born
here and chose not to leave and birthed you

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.640
here into this system where there is taxes.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.480
So you do have recourse.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.580
Your parents had recourse.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.989
There are options here.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:27.090
And then number four, you can also lobby to
get elected officials who agree that taxation

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.090
is theft.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.900
And if they get elected, they can try to eliminate
taxes.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.379
So it's not theft and it's not slavery.

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:40.110
Now, the bigger picture, of course, is there
is no way to have a civilized society without

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.120
taxes.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:49.959
Anthropological research and other sociological
research tells us that what usually they talk

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:52.610
about 150, it's called the Dunbar number.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:04:00.629
When you get to 150 people organizing 150
people, you need some centralization and some

00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:04.659
decisions that are made thinking of the group
as a collective.

00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:10.390
If you don't, you have untenable situations
that would prevent Homo sapiens from ever

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.470
advancing to the point at which we are now.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.640
Ideas of every road can be private.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.650
And you know, you build a road and then you
just charge people to go on it.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:23.400
And every road is private or police is private
and fire is private.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.889
These things, these things quite literally
do not work.

00:04:25.889 --> 00:04:28.620
Once you get beyond groups of 150 people.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:34.520
And so these folks are living in a complete
and total fantasy world.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.979
Usually you don't hear straight up taxation
is theft from elected officials in the House

00:04:38.979 --> 00:04:40.310
of Representatives.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:45.770
You hear it more from activists, you hear
it more from anti-tax groups or libertarian

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:46.770
groups.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:51.810
But to straight up here, taxation is theft
from someone in a position of power like this

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.990
really shows us the degree of radicalization
in the current Republican Congress.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.410
And it is very, very scary.

